A||||7||GT Bastard||Here's a pic of the  clutch I'm using for my 3.2 ||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||02-22-2001||06:57 PM||||Thanks to Trav(1FST2M6) at <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  for making it possible.  It's a "Kush-Lok" Type, Organic Lining, Marcel Drive Plate, Solid Hub, Street-Performance Clutch Disc. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Clutch1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Clutch2.jpg"> <P>Taken from <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  "A progressive engagement clutch disc having a compressible clutch plate assembly mounted between the clutch flywheel and pressure plate. The clutch plate assembly has a pair of outer aluminum, heat dissipating plates, a center wave spring plate coaxially mounted on a hub for axial movement relative to one another and to the hub, and clutch facings on the outer sides of the outer plates engagable with clutch facings on the flywheel and pressure plate. During clutch engagement, the clutch plate assembly and its spring are progressively compressed between the flywheel and pressure plate until the clutch plates are firmly gripped between the flywheel and pressure plate to permit torque transmission through the clutch without chattering, excessive stress on the clutch or transmission couplet to the clutch, and other problems associated with conventional clutches." <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-23-2001||08:07 AM||||i've driven cars with this unit and it's WAY easier to pilot than the 4 puck in there now! but you can still catch 3rd and 4th! thanks for the pics!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||02-23-2001||06:31 PM||||I hope so...  It looks like a torture device.  I think that 4-puck will make an awesome addition to my new coffee table.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MoneypitGT||03-08-2001||04:46 PM||||What kind of pressure plate are you using? I was going to use that clutch with a stock pressure plate, it is for a QUAD 4 with NOS, so the only thing I am concerned with is high rpm holding. Good or bad idea?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieroproject/moneypitgt.gif">   <B>Check out my site at:</B> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroproject" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroproject</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||5
Z||000004||GT Bastard||03-08-2001||04:52 PM||||Travis recommends the Beck&Arnley pressure plate(post auto part store can get them, but I think Trav recommended Napa) because it has a slightly higher clamp load.  The web site says they can be used with stock pressure plates.  The one currently in my SE is the Extreme pressure plate that Travis purchased through ACT(correct me if I'm wrong.)  When I do my new motor, I'm just using that disc with a stock pressure plate.  I think it would hold just fine under NOS.  That's what I'll be using mine for.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-09-2001||08:14 AM||||Napa Part # CA1914   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and yeah you'll be JUST fine with that disc and the NAPA pressure plate. just make sure you hafe the flywheels surfaced.. if not you'll wipe out the PP, the disc AND the flywheel. BlackGT had a 4puck and the NAPA PP and he could chirp 4th at 80+. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>  &lt;- GT Bastards car on the dyno...||||reg||1
Z||000006||MoneypitGT||03-09-2001||11:22 PM||||Thanks for the advice, I will be ordering that pp tomorrow, and flywheel is going out monday.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieroproject/moneypitgt.gif">   <B>Check out my site at:</B> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroproject" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroproject</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||03-10-2001||02:40 PM||||Can we see the rest of the parts? <P>Like the preasure plate and this compressible clutch plate assembly mounted between the clutch flywheel and pressure plate. Unless I am mistaken is there an additional part added in the mix of flywheel, clutch, preasure plate and TO bearing?<P>I am intrigued!||||reg||5
